    <%= erb :_nav %>
    <section class="content wrapper">
      <div>
        <img src="https://res.cloudinary.com/hptiz0can/image/upload/v1636253657/images/about_me/about_me_o0xfil.jpg">
      </div>
      <div class="description">
        Company Credentials:
        Small Business Enterprise- NJ
        Women Business Enterprise– NJ
        LGBTQ+ Business Enterprise- NJ
      </div>
      <div class="aboutMe">
        <p class="mainDescription">
          As a Principal Architect, Theodora Boyadjis brings over 20 years of experience to her work, shaped by both professional practice and a lifelong connection to architecture. Growing up working alongside her grandfather, a skilled finish carpenter, she developed an early appreciation for craftsmanship and the importance of detailed architectural elements in shaping a home. This foundation continues to inform her thoughtful, detail-driven approach.<br><br>

          After pursuing her education at NJIT, she built a strong technical and design foundation working on a range of high-end residential projects, where she refined her ability to translate concepts into cohesive, buildable designs. Over time, she expanded into leadership roles, taking on greater responsibility in managing projects, collaborating closely with clients, and guiding design direction from concept through execution. Her experience has also led to an extensive understanding of both federal and local building codes.<br><br>

          Through Theodora B Designs, she applies this depth of experience to residential and boutique commercial work, creating spaces that are both highly functional and visually enduring. With an emphasis on proportion, materiality, and craftsmanship, each project reflects a balance of clarity, intention, and timeless design.<br><br>

          Credentials: 
          
          <ul>
          <li>Registered Architect in NJ & NY</li>
          <li>LEED Accredited Professional</li>
        </ul>
        </p>


        <div style="margin-top: 32px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;">
          <h3>Sonia Parada</h3>
          <p>Sonia Parada is a Project Manager at Theodora Boyadjis Designs, where she contributes to the thoughtful development and execution of residential and commercial projects. With a detail-oriented approach, she is involved in all phases of design, from early concept through construction documentation, helping to ensure each project is both functional and refined.<br><br>
          Sonia holds a Bachelor’s degree in Architecture from the New Jersey Institute of Technology and brings a diverse range of experience across the industry. Her background includes roles in design, project management, and coordination at several architecture and design firms, where she gained a comprehensive understanding of technical documentation, consultant coordination, and client collaboration.
          Credentials:LEED Green Associate</p>
        </div>

        <div style="margin-top: 32px; padding-top: 24px; border-top: 1px solid #e0e0e0;">
          <h3>Jacob Sum</h3>
          <p>Jacob Sum is an Architectural drafter and Administrative Support at Theodora Boyadjis Designs, where he supports both the creative and operational aspects of the studio. In his role, he contributes to project development through design assistance, preparation of drawings, and administrative coordination, helping ensure the smooth progression of projects from concept through completion.<br><br>

            Jacob holds a Bachelor of Science in Landscape Architecture from the University of Florida, bringing a thoughtful perspective on site, environment, and the relationship between exterior and interior spaces. His academic foundation informs his detail-oriented approach and supports the firm’s emphasis on well-considered, cohesive design solution.<br><br>

            Working within a small, client-focused practice, Jacob plays a versatile role, supporting both the design team and day-to-day office functions. He is committed to maintaining high standards of organization and quality while continuing to develop his design skills and contribute to the firm’s thoughtful, detail-driven approach to architecture.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
